  "result": "**Findings:**\n\n1. **XSS vulnerability (main issue):** `render_profile_header` interpolates `name` directly into HTML without escaping. If `first_name`/`last_name` come from user-controlled data (profile fields typically are), a value like `<script>...</script>` gets rendered unescaped. Use `html.escape()` on `name` before embedding it in the `<h1>`, or use a templating engine with autoescaping instead of an f-string.\n\n2. **Redundant wrapper:** `get_display_name` just calls `build_display_name` with no added behavior \u2014 it's pure indirection. Collapse to a single function (pick one name, e.g. `build_display_name`) and call it directly from `render_profile_header`.\n\nNothing else stands out \u2014 the strip/format logic itself is correct for the stated goal.",
